{
 "_comment": [
  "Per-unit cast and attack timelines, transcribed from TFTraits (https://tftraits.com/cast-timelines/ and each",
  "https://tftraits.com/champions/<slug>/ page), retrieved 2026-09-20. TFTraits is a third party; its own",
  "disclaimer: \"not 100% accurate: they combine publicly available game data with gameplay observation\".",
  "The engine adopts these windows as a model rule with the standing of Azir's six-command mana lock and the",
  "0.5 s melee reposition: adopted, not verified in game. Re-transcribe when a patch changes animations.",
  "Seconds. attackDelay (from the start of an attack until it lands) and attackRecovery (after the landing",
  "until the unit can cast or attack again) are at base attack speed and scale with the attack animation;",
  "castAnimation (no attacks, no mana while it plays), channel (extra busy time after it) and effectAt (when",
  "the ability takes effect, from the start of the cast; absent = not stated) never scale.",
  "`base` is the form TFTraits lists first; `AD` / `AP` is the Adaptor's other form. A form takes its cast",
  "fields from its own entry when that has a castAnimation (or says noCastAnimation), its attack fields when",
  "it has an attackDelay, and the base entry's otherwise (tft.cast_timing_spec).",
  "What the engine reads: castAnimation, channel, effectAt, attackDelay, attackRecovery, and manaLock only",
  "under the lockRules that are a fixed time from the start of the cast (castAnimation, channel,",
  "untilEffectEnds). The other rules depend on the fight and belong to the unit's driver: effectDuration,",
  "shieldHolds (at most manaLock), empoweredAttacks (manaLock is at base attack speed), none. They are kept",
  "here, with lockNote, as the record of what the source says. A driver measures such a lock from the",
  "effect's own clock, which starts when the ability lands (effectAt into the cast, or the bin's cast time)",
  "and not from the start of the cast as this table's manaLock column does: the barrier, the flock and",
  "Frenzy begin at the landing, so the lock ends with them rather than while they are still up. Its end is",
  "therefore effectAt later than the figure here (Diana +0.66 s, Mama Beak +0.27 s, Brambleback +0.25 s) —",
  "seconds the unit spent inside the cast window anyway, and well inside the source's own precision.",
  "firstCast is TFTraits' own first cast of an itemless unit and `assumed` the bar, mana per attack, regen",
  "and attacks per second its card states for it: the acceptance reference of test_tft_cast_timing.",
  "noMana / noCastAnimation: the kit has no bar or no cast; nothing to time."
 ],
